%N A290348 Denominators of the Harary index for the n-halved cube graph.
%H A290348 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HalvedCubeGraph.html">Halved Cube Graph</a>.
%H A290348 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HararyIndex.html">Harary Index</a>.
%F A290348 a(n) = A000265(A330719(n)). - _Thomas Ordowski_, Mar 29 2025
%e A290348 The first few Harary indices are 0, 1, 6, 26, 100, 1096/3, 3920/3, 13936/3, 16544, 296256/5, ...; their denominators give this sequence. For example, a(6) = 3. [Corrected by _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 09 2026]
%t A290348 Table[-2^(n - 1) HarmonicNumber[n] - 2^(2 n - 1) Re[LerchPhi[2, 1, n + 1]], {n, 20}] // Denominator
%o A290348 (PARI) a(n) = my(x=denominator(sum(k=1, n, (2^(k-1)-1)/k))); x >> valuation(x, 2); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Oct 09 2026
